## Summary
MutualFundAuth-Web was already on the passbook theme (ink/parchment/gold tokens, Fraunces + IBM Plex fonts, dark ledger tables, dashed stamp badges, gold-left-border cards). The **only** thing not matching the Investment-Web Order/Investor pages (and the merged Scheme-Web PR #4) was the page header: it used a plain flat `.page-head` instead of the dark ink "cover band" with eyebrow + perforated dotted bottom edge.

This PR brings the headers to parity — visual only, no functionality/logic/API changes.

Global `.page-head` in `styles.scss` becomes the ink cover band:
```diff
 .page-head {
-  display: flex; ... padding: 28px 0 18px;
-  h1 { font-size: 26px; }
-  .sub { color: var(--text-muted); }
+  position: relative; overflow: hidden;
+  background: var(--ink); color: #F3EEDF; border-radius: 10px;
+  padding: 24px 26px 30px; margin: 24px 0 22px;
+  &::after { /* radial-gradient perforated bottom edge */ }
+  .eyebrow { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing:.14em; color:#B9C3DD; }
+  h1 { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; color: #F3EEDF; }
+  .sub { color: #B9C3DD; }
+  .btn-primary { /* gold-outlined pill on the ink band */ }
 }
```

Each page template (`login`, `register`, `users`, `pending`, `family`) gains a `<span class="eyebrow">` above the existing `<h1>`. Header action buttons ("New Group", "Approve All") now render as gold-outlined pills since they sit on the ink band (matching the Order page's on-cover button).

`ng build` passes. No CI/lint configured on the repo.


Link to Devin session: https://app.devin.ai/sessions/871dd1fafeb1491eac7b534e533716a2
Requested by: @shafiq0225

Two visual bugs: browser tabs showed double icons (emoji favicon + emoji in `<title>` rendered separately), and the floating header particles were generic white circles instead of basketballs.

## Changes

- **All HTML files** — strip leading emoji from `<title>` tags; the `<link rel="icon">` SVG emoji favicon is sufficient
- **`index.html` particles** — replace white circle CSS particles (`background + border-radius`) with `🏀` emoji nodes; use `font-size` per child to control size instead of `width/height`

```css
/* Before */
.particle {
  position: absolute; border-radius: 50%;
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.15); animation: floatUp linear infinite;
}
.particle:nth-child(1){ width:8px; height:8px; … }

/* After */
.particle {
  position: absolute; line-height: 1; user-select: none;
  animation: floatUp linear infinite;
}
.particle:nth-child(1){ font-size:16px; … }
```

```html
<!-- Before -->
<div class="particle"></div>…

<!-- After -->
<div class="particle">🏀</div>…
```
